edit:
git add .
git commit -m "edit"
OR
git commit -am "edit"    //-a means add
git push --set-upstream origin XXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

sync bitbucket:
get into the repo in local machine
$ git fetch
$ git pull      //sync
$ git status    //it shows which branch I'm on
$ git checkout release/xxx.xxx.~~~~~    //switch branch

fix an issue:
$ git status    //check modified files
$ git diff  ->  j  ->  q
$ git checkout -b "<new-branch-name>"    //create a new branch and switch to it
commit in VS code UI with messages
create a pull request in bitbucket

other commands:
$ git stash     //undo local changes

